    { q: 'How many days before finals should I start studying?', a: 'For a full exam period, begin serious revision about two weeks out. That leaves time to cover each subject twice: once to learn, once to test and patch gaps. Hard or heavily weighted subjects should start first.' },
    { q: 'Should I study one subject per day during finals?', a: 'Mixing two or three subjects a day usually beats one long block on a single subject. Interleaving keeps you fresher and strengthens your ability to switch between topics, which is what the exam demands.' },
